---
description: EF Core entity configuration, schemas, value objects and concurrency in Tadka
globs: src/**/Data/**/*.cs
alwaysApply: false
---

- Fluent API only: one `IEntityTypeConfiguration<T>` per entity in `Configurations/`. No data annotations on domain classes.
- Name the schema: `builder.ToTable("users", "identity")`. Never `HasOne` or `HasMany` toward another schema (ADR-008).
- Value objects are owned types: `builder.OwnsOne(...)`.
- Optimistic concurrency: `builder.Property<uint>("xmin").HasColumnName("xmin").HasColumnType("xid").IsRowVersion();` (ADR-012). A lost race is a 409.
- Read-only queries use `AsNoTracking()`. Reads right after a write stay on the primary (ADR-016).
- Migrations are per service, each in its own `Migrations/` folder. Never edit an applied migration.
